abstract: >-
  The Videha Digital Research Archive is a source-controlled digital humanities
  research environment for the connected histories, genealogy, literature,
  philosophy, places, texts and chronology of Mithila, Vajji and Anga across
  India and Nepal. Its publication layer provides permanent record URLs,
  citation exports, structured metadata, versioned datasets and checksum-based
  verification. Repository-authored software code is separately licensed under
  MIT; see RIGHTS.md for the full rights matrix.
